WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.660
From superhero action thrillers to down-to-earth
dramas and everything in between, here are

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:09.100
all the returning TV shows that will blow
you away in 2019.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.540
It looks like HBO’s True Detective is determined
to redeem itself after its unfortunate sophomore

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:15.040
slump.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:19.860
Featuring an all-new, all-star cast, the show’s
third season has a solid foundation from which

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.720
it can spin out into the mind-bending antics
we’ve all come to love and expect.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:28.260
The new episodes will follow state detective
Wayne Hays, his partner Roland, and schoolteacher

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:32.710
Amelia Reardon as they investigate the mysterious
disappearance of children in southern Missouri

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:33.880
during the 1980s.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.730
Much like the show’s groundbreaking first
season, the third installment will take place

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:42.240
across separate time periods, telling its
story through flashback and flashforward sequences.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:46.380
Judging by the teaser trailer HBO unveiled
for the new season, it seems that fans should

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:51.780
prepare themselves for a wild and emotional
ride when True Detective airs on January 3rd,

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:52.280
2019.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:55.000
Just who will win the Iron Throne?

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:59.980
That question has perplexed fantasy fans for
over twenty years, and should finally be answered

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:05.420
in 2019, when HBO airs the final season of
their wildly popular fantasy drama Game of

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:06.160
Thrones.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:11.079
These episodes, which may run up to two hours
long, based on reports, are also said to be

00:01:11.079 --> 00:01:15.789
the show's costliest yet, with one of their
huge battle set pieces allegedly taking a

00:01:15.789 --> 00:01:17.960
whopping 55 days to film.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.920
“Rest assured, your grace, you can count
on the Iron Bank's support.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.460
As soon as the gold arrives.”

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:30.920
Considering the show already has a huge body
count, it seems fairly safe to expect that

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.619
quite a few fan favorite characters could
end up biting the dust in the show's final

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:35.380
season, too.

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:39.600
Set your DVRs now, this isn’t going to be
a season you want to miss.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:45.220
2019 is gonna be a strange year, not least
because the third season of Netflix's sci-fi

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:48.220
hit Stranger Things is set to hit the streaming
platform.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:52.560
This time around, the story will span eight
episodes, down from the usual ten, and will

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:55.779
feature the Hawkins gang dealing with all-new
new "forces of evil."

00:01:55.779 --> 00:02:00.321
The series is also set to feature another
time jump, and will be set in the summer,

00:02:00.321 --> 00:02:02.320
a notable departure from the last two seasons.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:06.540
Although details are few and far between on
just where the show will go next plot-wise,

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:10.720
we do know a few details, including the fact
that it’ll feature more of season two fan

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:14.340
favorite Erica, as well as another likely
appearance from Kali, who should help to open

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:17.140
up more of the mystery surrounding Eleven's
past.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:18.560
“Sister.”

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:21.560
“Sister.”

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:27.240
Claire Foy may be leaving her post as Queen
Elizabeth for season three of Netflix’s

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:31.930
The Crown, but someone equally decorated will
assume the throne: Golden Globe-winning star

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:35.560
Olivia Colman, who’ll portray Her Royal
Highness in her later years.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:39.760
Season 3 will also see a slew of new cast
members take over other roles.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:43.810
These include Helena Bonham Carter, who’ll
play an older version of Princess Margaret;

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:48.680
Tobias Menzies taking on Matt Smith's role
as Prince Philip; and Ben Daniels becoming

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:49.980
the new Lord Snowdon.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:53.960
And that's just a hint of what’s to come
in the third season of The Crown, which will

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:57.780
chronicle events such as the Aberfan disaster,
Princess Margaret's five-year affair with

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:01.260
Roddy Llewellyn and Harold Wilson's tenure
as Prime Minister.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:05.840
Fans will also become acquainted with Camilla
Parker Bowles, the second wife of Prince Charles,

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:07.360
as well as the late Princess Diana.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:12.920
Big Little Lies was a massive hit for HBO
on its release last year, earning awards season

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:17.450
love across the board for its stars Reese
Witherspoon, Nicole Kidman, Shailene Woodley

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:18.240
and Laura Dern.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:22.810
Although the show was initially billed as
a limited series, it wasn't all that surprising

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:27.000
when HBO ordered a second season, to be written
by season one veteran David E. Kelley.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:31.440
Season two will also be drawn from a story
by Liane Moriarty, the author of the book

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.960
on which the series is based.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:38.200
The main cast is all set to return, with Transparent
and American Honey director Andrea Arnold

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.310
taking the director’s chair.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:43.740
If that’s not enough, Big Little Lies has
also added another huge name to its cast:

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:48.160
Meryl Streep, set to play the mother of Alexander
Skarsgard's character, Perry.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:53.500
Joe Penhall and David Fincher's gripping,
gory, and groovy '70s crime drama is coming

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:54.980
back for more later next year.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:04:00.140
Mindhunter was renewed by Netflix for a second
season right after the release of the first,

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:05.310
which chronicled the efforts of FBI agents
Holden Ford, Bill Tench and psychologist Wendy

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:08.900
Carr to establish the Behavioral Science Unit
at the FBI Academy.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:12.720
Interviewing serial killers in the hopes of
understanding the motivations behind their

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.020
grisly crimes was just part of the job.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.070
“You want truffles?

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.960
You gotta get in the dirt with the pigs.”

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:22.520
Fincher has previously told Billboard that
Mindhunter’s third season will center around

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:27.600
the notorious Atlanta child murders, which
took place between 1979 and 1981.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:33.900
Real-life FBI agent John E. Douglas, on whom
the show’s Holden character is based, profiled

00:04:33.909 --> 00:04:37.680
a man named Wayne Williams, believing him
to be one of the perpetrators.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:41.580
Williams eventually went to jail, but Douglas'
actions in getting him there resulted in him

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.080
being censured by the FBI.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:47.160
Given Holden’s breakdown at the end of the
first season, it wouldn’t be surprising

00:04:47.169 --> 00:04:50.729
if he becomes a little more radical in his
methods as the second progresses.

